# School Box environment -- copy to .env.school-box (gitignored, real
# secrets go there) alongside this file: `cp .env.school-box.example .env.school-box`
# then edit every value below. Referenced by school-box/compose/docker-compose.yml's
# `env_file: ../.env.school-box` on the api/sync-agent services.

# ── IDENTITY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This box's own identity, sent as sync.outbox's device_id (see
# backend/db/migrations/V029__sync_outbox.sql and
# school-box/sync-agent/cmd/main.go). Generate once per physical box,
# never reuse across boxes -- two boxes sharing an ID would corrupt the
# cloud's picture of which changes came from where.
SCHOOL_BOX_ID=changeme-generate-a-real-uuid

# The school's UUID in the central `schools` table (Central Cloud system
# of record) -- ask the Ministry/regional admin who provisions schools
# for this, it's not something a School Box generates itself.
SCHOOL_ID=changeme-ask-ministry-admin-for-this-schools-uuid

# Proves the SCHOOL_BOX_ID above to the cloud's /api/v1/sync/push and
# /pull endpoints (see backend/internal/sync/handler/device_auth.go) --
# a School Box is headless, so this is a shared secret, not a JWT a human
# logs in for. NOT generated here: run, once, from a machine with access
# to the Central Cloud database, before this box's first boot:
#   go run ./backend/cmd/provision-school-box -device-id <SCHOOL_BOX_ID above> -school-id <SCHOOL_ID above>
# It prints this value once (only its bcrypt hash is stored server-side,
# so a lost secret means re-running the command, not recovering it).
SCHOOL_BOX_SECRET=changeme-run-provision-school-box-and-paste-the-printed-secret

# ── SYNC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Central Cloud API's base URL. Must be reachable when the box HAS
# internet -- sync-agent tolerates it being unreachable (retries next
# interval, see sync-agent/internal/sync/agent.go), it just doesn't sync
# until it can reach this.
CLOUD_SYNC_URL=https://api.edugraph.et

# ── IMAGES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docker-compose.yml's services are all `image:`, not `build:` -- a
# School Box pulls pre-built images, it doesn't build from source on
# school hardware. These two are also the only vars in this file that
# docker-compose.yml itself interpolates (${ECR_REGISTRY}/edugraph-api:
# ${IMAGE_TAG}, etc.) rather than just passing through to a container's
# environment -- see scripts/install.sh and scripts/update.sh, which
# both pass `--env-file ../.env.school-box` for exactly this reason.
# Match whatever registry .github/workflows/ci.yml's `vars.ECR_REGISTRY`
# publishes to for a box with internet access; a box being provisioned
# offline needs images pre-loaded via `docker load` instead (see
# install.sh), in which case these still need to match the tags those
# loaded images actually carry.
ECR_REGISTRY=changeme-your-registry-host
IMAGE_TAG=latest

# ── DATABASE PASSWORDS ────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate real random passwords for a real deployment -- these are
# LAN-local (nothing here is exposed to the internet, see
# school-box/config/Caddyfile), but "LAN-local" is not "no access
# control": anyone on the school's network, or anyone with physical
# access to the box, is inside this trust boundary.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
NEO4J_PASSWORD=changeme

# ── AI (checklist 8.1: local-first by default) ───────────────
# Leave LLM_PROVIDER=local and GEMINI_API_KEY empty for a School Box --
# that's the entire point of this deployment (PRD §7.1: "the School Box
# solves this by making the entire platform -- including AI inference --
# run on local hardware with zero internet dependency"). Setting
# GEMINI_API_KEY here would work (the fallback logic in
# ai-service/app/utils/llm_provider.py tries whichever provider isn't
# primary too), but defeats the purpose of a box meant to run with no
# connectivity at all.
LLM_PROVIDER=local
GEMINI_API_KEY=
